#!/usr/bin/env ybm
# Verifies: SPEC.md §1 (CLI). The ybm CLI only accepts files with the `.ybm` extension.
# DECISIONS.md D-CLI-04: an invalid extension is treated as a file I/O error, diagnostic code E9002, exit code 1.
# This file's own extension is deliberately `.notybm`. Even though its content is
# grammatically correct, the CLI rejects it via the extension check before opening/
# lexing the file, so the print below should never execute (a side effect is left in
# place so execution would be detectable if it somehow did run).

print("this line must never execute: extension check happens before parsing")
